                <pb facs="0560" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.51/179: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cottrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-10T10:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                                1923—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:20
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>21. Referring to my cable of April 3, noon. The President has named Jorge Saenz,
                    Manager of the Bank of the Nation, and José <pb facs="0561" n="445"
                        xml:id="pg445"/> Mendieta, Manager of the National Bank, a Commission with
                    full powers to go to New York to arrange modifications in loan contract. They
                    leave April 26th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cottrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
